x86_64-linux  cxx1 writes the C1 and D1 forms of the constructors and destructors `P`, `Q`, `V`, `W`, `VB` and `H` define inside their classes, and `Dia`'s C2 beside its C1, where clang emits only the forms a use asks for (docs/CONFORMANCE.md, "An inline member function is a strong symbol"); and the guarded static local `kept`, which cxx1 names `_ZL11staticLocali.kept` with its own guard where Itanium spells `_ZZL11staticLocaliE4kept` and `_ZGVZ...` (docs/CONFORMANCE.md, "A static local keeps its own name in the object file"). Every declared name agrees.
x86_64-windows  the same static local, `?kept@?1??staticLocal@@YAHH@Z@4UP@@A` and its `$TSS0` guard in clang's spelling.
arm64-darwin  `V`'s and `VB`'s C1, which clang does not emit for a class built only as a base, and `Dia`'s C2 beside its C1 - the in-class rule above.
